-- Regression: a fixity annotation stranded above a directive must NOT leak
-- to a later definition. Here `@infixl 6` sits above an #EVAL directive, not
-- above a binary operator definition. It is reported as misplaced and
-- ignored; in particular `leakTarget` does NOT silently acquire fixity, so a
-- bare chain over it keeps the usual arity error (no default fixity).

@infixl 6
#EVAL 1

GIVEN p IS A NUMBER
      q IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
p leakTarget q MEANS p + q

-- Must error: leakTarget has no fixity of its own, and the stray @infixl 6
-- above the directive must not have reached it.
#EVAL 1 leakTarget 2 leakTarget 3
